    {
      "id": "web",
      "blogSlug": "sedef-adasi",
      "titles": {
        "tr": "Web",
        "en": "Web"
      },
      "contents": {
        "tr": "<p>Bireysel bir çalışmadır. Web sitesi düzenleme ve iyileştirme çalışmaları devam etmektedir. </p>\n\n<hr />\n\n<h3>Dragos'tan Prens Adaları ve Marmara Canlı Görüntüsü</h3>\n\n<p>Kartal - Sedef Adası rotasındaki  deniz ve hava koşullarını canlı olarak izleyebilirsiniz.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://istanbuluseyret.ibb.gov.tr/dragos-yeni\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color:#0066cc;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:bold;\">Canlı Kamera Yayını için tıklayınız</a><br />\n<small>(İBB sistem kısıtlamaları nedeniyle canlı yayın yalnızca yeni sekmede izlenebilmektedir.)</small></p>",
        "en": "<p>This is a personal project. Website editing and improvement work is ongoing. </p>\n\n<hr />\n\n<h3>Live View of the Princes' Islands and Marmara from Dragos</h3>\n\n<p>You can watch the sea and weather conditions on the Kartal - Sedef Island route live.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://istanbuluseyret.ibb.gov.tr/dragos-yeni\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color:#0066cc;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:bold;\">Click here for the live camera broadcast</a><br />\n<small>(Due to İBB system restrictions, the live broadcast can only be viewed in a new tab.)</small></p>"
      },
      "categories": {
        "tr": [],
        "en": []
      },
      "publishedAt": "2026-05-01T00:00:00.000Z",
      "type": "PAGE",
      "isSimulated": true
    },
    {
      "id": "kis_baskadir",
      "blogSlug": "sedefadasinda-kis-baskadir",
      "titles": {
        "tr": "Lodosun ve Sessizliğin Kış Günlüğü",
        "en": "Winter Diary of Lodos and Silence"
      },
      "contents": {
        "tr": "<div class=\"post-hero-image\">\n<img src=\"/sedef_winter1.JPG\" alt=\"Sedefadası Kış\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:420px;object-fit:cover;border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:1.5rem;\" />\n</div>\n<p>Yaz kalabalıkları şehre çekildiğinde, iskele meydanı, yollar, plajlar bomboş kaldığında Sedef Adası bambaşka bir ruha bürünür. Sadece lodosun uğultusu, kayalara sert vuran dalgalar ve gökyüzünde daireler çizen martıların çığlıkları kalır. Tek tük evlerin bacalarından tüten odun sobası dumanları, kışın adada kalan birkaç yalnız yüreğin sıcak yuvasını müjdeler. Kış gecelerinde küçük bir odada okunan kitapların, demlenen çayların tadı hiçbir yerde bulunmaz. Kışın sürprizi ise bir gün de olsa adayı bembeyaz karla kaplar...</p>\n<div style=\"margin-top:1.5rem;\">\n<img src=\"/sedef_winter21.JPG\" alt=\"Sedefadası Kış\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:420px;object-fit:cover;border-radius:12px;\" />\n</div>",
        "en": "<div class=\"post-hero-image\">\n<img src=\"/sedef_winter1.JPG\" alt=\"Sedefada Winter\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:420px;object-fit:cover;border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:1.5rem;\" />\n</div>\n<p>When the summer crowds return to the city and the pier square, roads, and beaches become empty, Sedef Island takes on a completely different spirit. Only the moan of the lodos wind, waves pounding the rocks, and the cries of seagulls circling in the sky remain. Wood stove smoke rising from the chimneys of the few scattered houses heralds the warm hearths of the few lonely hearts who stay on the island in winter. The taste of books read in a small room and tea brewed on winter nights cannot be found anywhere else. The surprise of winter is when, even for one day, the island is covered in pure white snow...</p>\n<div style=\"margin-top:1.5rem;\">\n<img src=\"/sedef_winter21.JPG\" alt=\"Sedefada Winter\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:420px;object-fit:cover;border-radius:12px;\" />\n</div>"
      },
      "categories": {
        "tr": [],
        "en": []
      },
      "publishedAt": "2026-05-01T00:00:00.000Z",
      "type": "POST",
      "isSimulated": true
    },
    {
      "id": "filmler",
      "blogSlug": "filmler",
      "titles": {
        "tr": "Sedef Adası Belgeseli ve Tarihi Video Arşivi",
        "en": "Sedef Island Documentary and Historical Video Archive"
      },
      "contents": {
        "tr": "<p>Çocukluğumuzun, gençliğimizin güzel anıları Sedefadası'nda şekillendi: yüzdük, koştuk, uzun sohbetler ettik, eğlenceler düzenledik... Adamızın tarihine, güzelliğine ve anılarına ait videolar aşağıda yer almaktadır.</p>\n<div style=\"position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%;height:0;overflow:hidden;max-width:100%;\">\n<iframe style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/8ag8qLfzCNQ\" title=\"Sedef Adası Tarihi Belgeseli\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div>\n<div style=\"position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%;height:0;overflow:hidden;max-width:100%;\">\n<iframe style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/ADpjA_MiOLs\" title=\"Sedef Adası Video 2\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div>\n<div style=\"position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%;height:0;overflow:hidden;max-width:100%;\">\n<iframe style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/NLZFuLCiFpY\" title=\"Sedef Adası Video 3\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div>",
        "en": "<p>The beautiful memories of our childhood and youth were shaped on Sedef Island: we swam, ran, held long conversations, and organized celebrations... Videos related to our island’s history, beauty, and memories are shown below.</p>\n<div style=\"position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%;height:0;overflow:hidden;max-width:100%;\">\n<iframe style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/8ag8qLfzCNQ\" title=\"Sedef Island Historical Documentary\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div>\n<div style=\"position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%;height:0;overflow:hidden;max-width:100%;\">\n<iframe style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/ADpjA_MiOLs\" title=\"Sedef Island Video 2\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div>\n<div style=\"position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%;height:0;overflow:hidden;max-width:100%;\">\n<iframe style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/NLZFuLCiFpY\" title=\"Sedef Island Video 3\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div>"
      },
      "categories": {
        "tr": [],
        "en": []
      },
      "publishedAt": "2026-05-01T00:00:00.000Z",
      "type": "POST",
      "isSimulated": true
    },
    {
      "id": "yerlesim",
      "blogSlug": "yerlesim-ve-emlak",
      "titles": {
        "tr": "Anılar",
        "en": "Memories"
      },
      "contents": {
        "tr": "<p>Çocukluğumuzun, gençliğimizin güzel anıları Sedef Adası'nda şekillendi: yüzdük, koştuk, uzun sohbetler ettik, eğlenceler düzenledik... </p>\n<p>Adamızda uzun yıllar geçirmiş, kattıkları güzelliklerle hatıralarımızda yer tutan ve bizlere ışık olan büyüklerimizi şükranla anıyoruz. Şiir gecelerinin kahkahalı dostları, bol sohbetli komşuları, adanın güneydoğusunda bir mercan veya kırlangıcı olta başında saatlerce bekleyen bir baba, yaşlı çiftlerin sakin akşam yürüyüşü, yazarın tek başına kayalıklardan ufukları seyri, balerinin güneşin doğuşunu kutsayan dansı, bazı evlerden yayılan canlı müziğin coşkusu, gecesini gündüzüne katan bekçilerimizin, emek verenlerimizin güler yüzlü, dostça çabası... Ve her köşesinde özgür martılar. Sedef Adası'nın ruhunu burada yaşayanlar bilir.</p>\n<p> Yasemin Giritli İnceoğlu (*) şöyle aktarıyor anılarını, duygularını: Babam ve annem İstanbul Üniversitesi Hukuk Fakültesi’nde sınıf arkadaşlarıymış. Dört yıllık arkadaşlığın ardından evlenmişler. Evliliklerinden iki çocukları olmuş; biri ağabeyim Ahmet Rıza, ikincisi de benim. Annem 61 yıl süren evlilikleri boyunca babamın hep sağ kolu oldu. İsmet Giritli’yi İsmet Giritli yapan Suna (Ağaoğlu) Giritli’dir. Babam 1961 Anayasası’nı hazırlayan bilim adamlarından biri oldu. Çocuklarıyla, eşiyle, dostlarıyla ilişkilerine daima değer veren, aydın bir insandı. Neşesi, esprileri, sosyalliği ve yardımseverliği ile tanınırdı. Hayatı ondan öğrendim diyebilirim... 1961’de Nişantaşı’nda doğdum ve Sedef Adası’yla tanışmam üç yaşındayken oldu. Annemin dayısının kızı, Türkiye’nin ilk kadın avukatı Süreyya Ağaoğlu Ada’da oturuyordu ve biz de yazın evine misafir olarak geliyorduk. </p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/teyzeveyasemin01.jpg\" alt=\"Teyzemle\" style=\"display:block;margin:20px auto;max-width:80%;height:auto;border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);\" />\n\n<p>Bu gidiş gelişlerde, annem Ada’ya âşık oldu ve bu evi alma konusunda babama ısrarcı oldu. 1965 yılında bu eve yerleştik. Annem Azeri kökenli olduğu için çok güzel Kafkas Pilavı yapardı. Her hafta sonu Ada’da 'Suna’nın Kafkas Pilavı' partileri verilirdi. Bu partilere konsoloslar, büyükelçiler, akademisyenler, sanatçılar, ada halkı, herkes davetliydi. Her hafta sonu evimiz cıvıl cıvıldı; dolup taşardı… Evimiz Türkiye’nin televizyon ile tanıştığı dönemlerde de şen şakraktı. Babam 1968 -1969 yıllarında TRT yönetim kurulu başkanıydı. Böyle olunca haliyle, Adalar’da ilk televizyon denemesi de Sedef Adası’nda, bizim evde oldu. Salonumuza televizyon kuruldu. Bütün çocuklar evimize gelir, salonun ortasında oturur, siyah - beyaz deneme yayınlarını seyrederlerdi... Bir kooperatif plajımız vardı. Üç-dört kuşak bu plajda bir aradaydık; çocuklar, anneler, torunlar, anneanneler hep birlikte orada yüzerdik… Orası bir sosyalleşme yeriydi. Çünkü Ada’da sinema, tiyatro yoktu. İnsanlar ya birbirlerinin evinde bir akşam yemeğinde ya da bu plajlarda bir araya gelirdi... Şehre o kadar yakın, ama bir o kadar da uzağız. Burada yaşayanlar son derece tevazu sahibi insanlar. Yaz aylarımızı eşim Bülent ve kızım Deniz’le halen Sedef Adası’nda geçiriyoruz. Sedef Adası, kendimi en iyi, en mutlu hissettiğim bir yer. Kısacası, burası benim cennetim!...</p>\n<p>(*): <a href=\"https://www.yasemininceoglu.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color:#0066cc;text-decoration:underline;\">Yasemin Giritli İnceoğlu</a></p>\n\n<p>",
        "en": "<p>The happiest memories of our childhood and youth were shaped on Sedef Island: we swam, we ran, we had long conversations, and we celebrated with joyful gatherings.</p>\n<p>We are grateful to the elders who lived on the island for many years and left their warmth in our memories. There were friends laughing at poetry evenings, neighbors who talked for hours, fathers waiting patiently by the sea for fish or swallows, elderly couples walking quietly in the evening, a writer gazing alone toward the horizon from the rocks, a ballerina greeting the sunrise with her dance, the sound of live music spilling from some houses, and the friendly, hardworking island guards who kept the nights alive. Free seagulls filled every corner. The people who live here know the spirit of Sedef Island.</p>\n<p> Aykut and Melahat Behlil... Their daughter Melis was still a baby. Many of us remember their quiet, peaceful evening walks toward the tennis court. And of course, always with them was Paşa, their dog and everyone's favorite.</p>\n<p> Ms. Melahat Behlil recalls the early years on the island as follows: </p>\n<p>My father and mother were very old friends of Rey’an Hanım and Şehsuvar Bey. They had approached my parents and said, “We are trying to gather old friends on an island like this, we are establishing a cooperative and so on. Would you consider joining?”... My parents liked the idea, and that is how they decided… I remember that we came for the first time in 1961. Because the coup took place in 1960, and the Yassıada trials ended in 1961. We were living in Ankara at the time, and my father said, </p>\n<p>“Come on, let us leave here as soon as possible. These people have questionable intentions. Let us return home…” </p>\n<p>That is how I remember that 1961 was our first visit to the island. Among my earliest memories of Sedef Island are our days at Mahama. Do you know Mahama? </p>\n<p>Rey’an Hanım, Şehsuvar Bey, and the architect Kadri Eroğan told their close friend Malike Akbay: </p>\n<p>“There is a wonderful place here. You know many people, and the social circle is delightful…” </p>\n<p>She herself was a delightful woman as well… </p>\n<p>“Come and run this place…” </p>\n<p>“Oh, how could I? I have never worked in such a business before; I do not know anything about these things...” </p>\n<p>“You can do it,” they said. “We will help you...” </p>\n<p>So, in a completely amateur and informal way, Malike Akbay began operating this restaurant on the island. She named it “Mahama,” formed from the initials of Malike Akbay, her daughter Hümeyra (Akbay), the singer and actress, and her late husband Muvaffak Akbay... </p>\n<p>When Mahama first opened, island residents gathered there frequently. Malike Hanım managed the place with remarkable warmth and charm. Cassette tapes would be brought from the DJs and nightclubs of Büyükada, and wonderful music would be played there. Malike Hanım was an exceptionally warm and sincere person. For example, whenever she found herself in a tight spot, she would say, “Oh, hurry, we've run out of rakı. Could you bring some from home?” and off we would go to fetch it… I even remember that Ayda, the daughter of Aunt Melek, and I occasionally helped with table service when needed… So it all began and continued in a very intimate and friendly atmosphere. The menu was limited, perhaps pasta and a few other dishes, but it attracted a wonderful clientele. On one occasion, even Princess Fazile, the daughter of Princess Hanzade, celebrated her birthday there. It continued for several years. It was a delightful place, truly lovely. I am not sure whether someone else operated it in between, but later Nuran Hanım came and took it over… </p>\n<p></p>\n<p>Yasemin Giritli İnceoğlu (*) also shares her memories and feelings: My father and mother were classmates at Istanbul University Faculty of Law. They married after four years of friendship and had two children: my older brother Ahmet Rıza and me. During their 61-year marriage, my mother was always my father's right hand. It was Suna (Ağaoğlu) Giritli who made İsmet Giritli who he was. My father became one of the scholars who prepared the 1961 Constitution. He was a bright person who always valued his relationships with his children, his spouse, and his friends. He was known for his joy, humor, sociability, and generosity. I can say I learned life from him... I was born in 1961 in Nişantaşı, and I first met Sedef Island when I was three years old. My mother's uncle's daughter, Süreyya Ağaoğlu, Turkey's first female lawyer, lived on the island, and we visited her house every summer.</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/teyzeveyasemin01.jpg\" alt=\"With my aunt\" style=\"display:block;margin:20px auto;max-width:80%;height:auto;border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);\" />\n\n<p>On those visits, my mother fell in love with the island and insisted that my father buy this house. We moved in during 1965. Because my mother was of Azeri heritage, she cooked delicious Caucasian pilaf. Every weekend on the island there were \"Suna's Caucasian Pilaf\" parties. Diplomats, ambassadors, academics, artists, and island residents were all invited. Our house was full of life and laughter every weekend. During the time when television was just arriving in Turkey, our home was always lively. My father served as the chairman of the TRT board in 1968–1969, so naturally the first television experiments in the Princes' Islands happened at our house. A TV was set up in our living room. All the children would come, sit in the middle of the room, and watch the black-and-white test broadcasts.</p>\n<p>We had a cooperative beach. Three or four generations came together there: children, mothers, grandchildren, grandmothers—we all swam together. It was a place to socialize because the island had no cinema or theater. People came together either for an evening meal at someone’s house or on those beaches. We were so close to the city, yet at the same time we felt far away. The people who live here are extremely humble. My husband Bülent, my daughter Deniz, and I still spend our summers on Sedef Island. It is the place where I feel my best and happiest. In short, this is my paradise!</p>\n<p>(*): <a href=\"https://www.yasemininceoglu.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color:#0066cc;text-decoration:underline;\">Yasemin Giritli İnceoğlu</a></p>\n\n<p>"
      },
